WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
Tracepad. Understand it. Build it. Explain it.

2
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:09.475
A local Python workspace, built for deliberate practice.

3
00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:15.351
Keep each interview in its own saved project.

4
00:00:15.351 --> 00:00:23.205
Organize your solution into real, importable Python modules.

5
00:00:23.205 --> 00:00:30.083
Run Python locally. Inspect the output beside your code.

6
00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:37.693
Six named tests. Normal inputs and edge cases, all passing.

7
00:00:37.693 --> 00:00:44.758
Trace the state by hand, one step at a time.

8
00:00:44.758 --> 00:00:50.825
Sketch the approach before reaching for code.

9
00:00:50.825 --> 00:01:00.458
Keep assumptions, tradeoffs, and complexity notes with your work.

10
00:01:00.458 --> 00:01:06.321
Supply multiline input before the program runs.

11
00:01:06.321 --> 00:01:13.213
The Python standard library is available locally.

12
00:01:13.213 --> 00:01:20.421
A real exception, with its traceback ready to inspect.

13
00:01:20.421 --> 00:01:27.529
Correct the boundary and run again

14
00:01:27.529 --> 00:01:36.914
Stop an infinite loop without losing the workspace

15
00:01:36.914 --> 00:01:42.313
Choose a focused topic drill or a complete mock interview.

16
00:01:42.313 --> 00:01:51.199
A strict sixty-minute mock starts with a blank editor.

17
00:01:51.199 --> 00:01:56.450
No pause or reset. This edited demo uses the real clock.

18
00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:01.509
Clarify the contract before you implement it.

19
00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:11.111
Write the object model and explain the approach.

20
00:02:11.111 --> 00:02:20.036
Prepared code is pasted here to keep the walkthrough short.

21
00:02:20.036 --> 00:02:26.672
The app executes that code and captures real output.

22
00:02:26.672 --> 00:02:33.428
Opt in: an external assistant can add live requirements via MCP.

23
00:02:33.428 --> 00:02:42.093
The coach reads the current work, then sends a new requirement.

24
00:02:42.093 --> 00:02:53.028
Acknowledge the change and extend the implementation.

25
00:02:53.028 --> 00:02:59.594
A custom test checks the new borrower view.

26
00:02:59.594 --> 00:03:06.168
Submit the code, reasoning, and test evidence together.

27
00:03:06.168 --> 00:03:10.724
The original baseline is fixed. All six checks pass.

28
00:03:10.724 --> 00:03:16.781
Review the time actually spent in each interview stage.

29
00:03:16.781 --> 00:03:22.850
Tracepad sends the submitted code and run evidence to the MCP coach.

30
00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:31.441
The external coach returns a review grounded in those results.

31
00:03:31.441 --> 00:03:37.315
Ask your connected assistant for a focused OOP question.

32
00:03:37.315 --> 00:03:44.718
An original question arrives with examples and named checks.

33
00:03:44.718 --> 00:03:54.433
Validate the supplied reference solution before starting.

34
00:03:54.433 --> 00:03:59.990
A failing check exposes shared mutable state

35
00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:05.869
Request a hint. The coach can inspect the current code and failures.

36
00:04:05.869 --> 00:04:15.980
A contextual hint arrives directly in the Interview panel.

37
00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:22.876
Independent instance state and defensive copies: five checks pass.

38
00:04:22.876 --> 00:04:29.482
Save the practice record with the help that was used

39
00:04:29.482 --> 00:04:34.766
A complete light theme, including the review.

40
00:04:34.766 --> 00:04:40.002
Choose your theme. Your projects and preferences stay local.

41
00:04:40.002 --> 00:04:43.557
Refresh and resume the saved project

42
00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:48.600
Local by default. Optional MCP coaching. github.com/sidkolapalli/TracePad
